From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Alsey Coleman Miller <alseycmiller@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 00:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] [Threading] Make the 32-bit Linux once lock recursive

On 32-bit Linux there is no room for a per-once lock, so once_slow
serialises every swift::once behind one global mutex, and holds it while
the initializer runs. An initializer that runs another once then waits
on itself. swift_getCanonicalPrespecializedGenericMetadata does exactly
that: its cacheCanonicalSpecializedMetadata initializer calls getCache,
which runs its own once. Prespecialization is turned off for 32-bit ARM
only, and on 32-bit PowerPC every Swift program hangs there before main.

Make the lock recursive. Re-entry is only ever for a different once: the
predicate is still checked under the lock, and a once whose initializer
re-enters itself was a bug before. The mutex is set up through
pthread_once since musl has no static initializer for a recursive one.
---
--- a/lib/Threading/Linux.cpp
+++ b/lib/Threading/Linux.cpp
@@ -38,7 +38,20 @@
 MainThreadRememberer rememberer;
 
 #if !defined(__LP64__) && !defined(_LP64)
-pthread_mutex_t once_mutex = PTHREAD_MUTEX_INITIALIZER;
+// One lock serves every once on 32-bit, and a once's initializer may run
+// another once (generic metadata prespecialization does), so the lock has
+// to be recursive. It is set up through pthread_once because musl has no
+// static initializer for a recursive mutex.
+pthread_mutex_t once_mutex;
+pthread_once_t once_mutex_ready = PTHREAD_ONCE_INIT;
+
+void init_once_mutex() {
+  pthread_mutexattr_t attr;
+  pthread_mutexattr_init(&attr);
+  pthread_mutexattr_settype(&attr, PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE);
+  pthread_mutex_init(&once_mutex, &attr);
+  pthread_mutexattr_destroy(&attr);
+}
 #endif
 
 #pragma clang diagnostic pop
@@ -58,6 +71,7 @@
 #if defined(__LP64__) || defined(_LP64)
   linux::ulock_lock(&predicate.lock);
 #else
+  pthread_once(&once_mutex_ready, init_once_mutex);
   pthread_mutex_lock(&once_mutex);
 #endif
   if (predicate.flag.load(std::memory_order_acquire) == 0) {
